## Notes

1. **No new VALID findings** in this probe batch. All 40 probe samples (spanning ~27 hours) reconfirm the 5 accepted findings (A1–A5) as STABLE with no regression.

2. **No HOLD candidates.** The prior HOLD items (superAdmin token-minting, Engage portal IDOR, cross-origin write on orgs controller) remain unresolved but were not reprobed in this batch — no new evidence to promote them.

3. **Probe quality note:** Several probe entries contain backtick-appended URLs (e.g., `` /v1/global/regions` ``) and undefined variable substitutions (`$s`, `$p`, `<AUTHORIZED_UUID>`). These are scanner-side probe errors that return 400/404 — they do not represent new leads and should not be triaged.

4. **Regression monitoring:** `v1/global/regions` returned 400 in all samples this batch (down from the historical 200-with-garbage-token pattern). This is expected — the 400 is the no-auth baseline; the scheme-bypass requires a malformed `Bearer x` header which these particular probes did not send. A2 remains valid per the knowledge base. If future probes explicitly send `Bearer x` and receive 400 consistently, flag as potential regression.

---

**Reporting channel:** Spare security channel (per scope.yml, TBD — operator has not yet confirmed public disclosure channel).

**Next action:** Continue passive monitoring. No new report to file this cycle.
